# What NOT to send to the Docker build context. The console image (packages/docker/console.Dockerfile) builds from
# source inside the image, so host build output and installed deps must stay out — the builder regenerates
# them for the image's platform. Keeping this tight also makes the context upload fast.

# Installed dependencies — the builder runs its own `bun install` (host node_modules would be the wrong
# platform and would shadow the fresh install).
**/node_modules

# Build artifacts — regenerated in the builder. Covers packages/sdk/dist, apps/console/{dist,dist-server},
# and the daemon's Go output.
**/dist
**/dist-server
**/.next
daemon/bin
packages/sdk/npm

# Local runtime state (the auth SQLite lives in a mounted volume, never in the image).
**/.data

# VCS / CI / tooling — not needed to build the app.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode

# Logs and OS cruft.
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store

# Compose files and this ignore file itself.
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

# Env / secrets never enter the image — but keep the committed example so it is easy to reference.
# The `**/` prefix is load-bearing: it matches .env at any depth, not just the root.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
